@startuml oscal-journey-activity
|Document Author|
start
:submit verbatim document\n(PDF/Word/spreadsheet-CSV/Markdown/text);
|System|
:normalize into consistent text (FR-001, FR-002);
:AI-assisted conversion to Trestle Markdown,\nchunked if needed (FR-018);
if (identifier collision (FR-013) or\nLLM error/timeout (FR-014)?) then (yes)
  :fail whole conversion, no partial output;
  |Document Author|
  :see specific, actionable error (SC-004);
  stop
else (no)
endif
if (any section not confidently mapped?) then (yes)
  :flag as unconvertible, keep rest (US1 Scenario 3);
else (no)
endif
:trestle structural/header validation (FR-003);
if (validation passes?) then (no)
  :surface specific validation error;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
|Compliance Officer / Auditor|
if (approval required? (FR-011)\nregulatory-standard, or first-time approval) then (yes)
  :review and approve;
else (no: already-approved custom-policy revision)
endif
|System|
:trestle import + author/assemble\n-> OSCAL Catalog + Profile (US2, FR-004, FR-009);
if (assembly fails against validated Markdown?) then (yes)
  :surface Trestle's specific failure (FR-010);
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:trestle profile-resolve\n-> fully Resolved OSCAL Catalog (US3, FR-005);
if (Profile references an unassembled Catalog?) then (yes)
  :surface clear error (US3 Scenario 2);
  stop
else (yes)
endif
|Document Author|
:Catalog, Profile, and Resolved Catalog available,\nkept distinct (FR-009);
stop
@enduml
